        "alt": "Graph of force against time, a line through the sensor readings. The force is steady at first (the student standing still), rises to a peak during the push, falls to zero at take-off, stays at zero while the student is in the air, then rises sharply at landing and settles back to its first value.",
        "caption": "Graph of force against time."
      },
      "graph-ms": {
        "alt": "Graph of force against time, a line through the sensor readings, with the area between the trace and the weight line from the start of the push to take-off (below the line counts as negative) shaded. The force is steady at first (the student standing still), rises to a peak during the push, falls to zero at take-off, stays at zero while the student is in the air, then rises sharply at landing and settles back to its first value.",
        "caption": "Graph of force against time. Shaded: the area between the trace and the weight line from the start of the push to take-off (below the line counts as negative)."
      }
    }
